DCC means Direct Client to Client

The main things you can do with this are:
--> send and receive files
--> have a private conversation

----- ----- ----- ----- ------

[1]		SENDING FILES
Anyone who you chat with on Incorrigo Syx has the ability to send files as well. If...

(a)	... you are sending a file to someone else, they will receive a request via the network in the form of a private message which is handled automatically
(b)	... someone else is sending you a file, then you will be prompted to either accept or decline the invitation
(c)	... the file is of a certain protected type - executables, for instance - then the recipient needs to use this command first --> /dccallow senders_nickname
	(/dccallow -senders_nickname) using the "-" character will remove the target matching your given nickname from the allow list for potentially harmful files

----- ----- ----- ----- -----

[2]		RECEIVING FILES
When someone attempts to send you a file, then a confirmation window will appear. This will show you the sender's nickname / IP address / file size / speculation of contents

If you are away from keyboard or simply deciding to ignore the file being sent, your IP address will not be revealed in any event except if you allow the sender to know your IP address by opening a peer-to-peer link between you and the other person. This can come in the form of a direct chat connection, a file transfer in either direction, or making use of your file server capabilities

----- ----- ----- ----- -----

[3]		DIRECT CHAT LINK
Using mIRC, you have the ability to create a direct link to chat with someone. Although it needs to be requested / accepted / established using private messages in both of your IRC session ... once the connection is made there is nothing that can be used to track or monitor conversations that people have had. In addition, it's unrealistic and virtually impossible to moderate such a conversation; with this in mind, the only one who has the capability of moderation is yourself and - no matter if you're still connected to the network or not - the direct link between yourself and the one you're chatting with may continue until one of you uses the option to make the ongoing link closed

You must remember that it is completely impossible for us to, nor make such an attempt at moderation, once you have established a direct link like this -- and it will make both sides' real IP / hostname - things which are hidden on Incorrigo Syx automatically - available to one another. Hence the term: Direct Client to Client
